 "relevance_note": "One cohort member (Table 1, S.No 8) is reported individually with an ITGB2 variant and diagnosis LAD1: \"**Gene** ITGB2 **Zygosity:** Homozygous\".",
 "method_note": "Single-centre retrospective PID case series (43 suspected, 20 confirmed). Only Table 1 S.No 8 is in scope (ITGB2, final diagnosis 'LAD1'); S.No 7 (FERMT3, 'LAD3') and S.No 9 ('LAD2', no gene tested, CD11C deficiency) are other LAD types without an ITGB2 variant or LAD-I diagnosis and get no rows. Label from the bare-number 'S.No' column (cell printed '8.'). Values transcribed by hand from the one row; spans checked verbatim by script. The 'Age/Sex' column (7 mo) is not defined; the methods list 'age at presentation', so it was not recorded as age at last evaluation. The variant cell labels 'c.134G > A' as 'Genomic coordinate (GRCh37/hg19)'; it is a cDNA description, so genomic_coordinates_as_stated is null; no transcript printed. Variant type 'Nonsense' is printed in the patient's own cell. The cohort-level statement 'A pathogenic gene variant was identified in 17 (85%) of the 20 confirmed cases' does not name which 17, so pathogenicity is not reported. n_patients_reported left null: the authors give LAD 3/20 but no count of ITGB2 carriers. Country left 'not reported': the study is at a hospital in Karachi, Pakistan, but the patient's own origin is not stated. Immunoglobulin and lymphocyte values printed for this patient (e.g. IgG:4.02 (6.5–16)) were not turned into features because the paper does not call them abnormal. Discussion statement that vaccinated cases have not developed vaccine disease refers to 'almost all cases', not a named group including this patient, so BCG complications stay not reported. 'skin rash' is not counted as a skin infection. No contradictions found.",
